      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "TING K'uei-ch'u 丁魁楚 (T. 光三), d. Mar. 3, 1647, Ming general, was a native of Yungch'êng, Honan. He passed the chin-shih examination in 1616. After several promotions he was appointed (1631) governor, stationed at Paoting, and three years later (1634) was made junior vice-president of the Board of War.",
          "source": "eccp-3656381",
